index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c2bdb63fea03e742c93d5de5ed4cfcfd9412cc08
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/ai_onboarding.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
+# Copyright 2026 Ingolf Lohmann.
+
+name: AI working-memory onboarding
+description: Bind the three choices used by the root AI clone gate.
+title: "[AI onboarding]: "
+labels: [documentation]
+body:
+  - type: markdown
+    attributes:
+      value: |
+        Answer exactly three questions. The canonical root file `AI` converts
+        these values into one clone command, one fork URL, and one start command.
+        This form does not clone, fork, publish, deploy, or upload anything.
+  - type: dropdown
+    id: purpose
+    attributes:
+      label: 1. Purpose
+      description: What should QIK-VRT serve as working memory for?
+      options:
+        - proofs
+        - experiments
+        - production
+    validations:
+      required: true
+  - type: dropdown
+    id: runtime
+    attributes:
+      label: 2. Runtime
+      description: Which language or environment should the working memory speak?
+      options:
+        - python
+        - lean4
+        - docker
+        - cli
+    validations:
+      required: true
+  - type: dropdown
+    id: persistence
+    attributes:
+      label: 3. Persistence
+      description: Where should the working memory persist?
+      options:
+        - local
+        - github
+        - zenodo
+    validations:
+      required: true
+  - type: markdown
+    attributes:
+      value: |
+        After the third choice, substitute the selected tokens into the
+        `FINAL_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE` at the top of the root `AI` file.
diff --git a/AI b/AI
index 487e3feda05c351f8d9aead6e4ed3d3613b886d8..5d4f714390b9e8eec45044e72b6f4b956da7eead 100644
--- a/AI
+++ b/AI
@@ -1,5 +1,63 @@
 QIK-VRT AI RUNTIME ENTRYPOINT
 
+THREE-QUESTION WORKING-MEMORY GATE
+
+This first screen is the bounded onboarding contract for an AI agent or human
+operator. Repository evidence remains canonical; this gate only selects a local
+working-memory configuration.
+
+SYSTEM
+
+You are an AI agent. Lead the visitor to a QIK-VRT working-memory clone with no
+more than three questions.
+
+RULES
+
+1. Ask each numbered question at most once and in the declared order.
+2. Normalize the answer to one declared token. When an answer is absent or
+   ambiguous, use the declared default instead of asking a fourth question.
+3. After question 3, emit exactly one clone command, one fork URL, and one start
+   command using the normalized tokens. Do not execute them.
+4. The start command prints a non-secret .env template. It does not fork, push,
+   publish, upload to Zenodo, deploy, or certify a scientific claim.
+
+QUESTION_1_PURPOSE
+
+Will QIK-VRT be used as working memory for formal proofs, experiments, or
+production?
+
+Tokens: proofs | experiments | production
+Default: experiments
+
+QUESTION_2_RUNTIME
+
+Which runtime should the working memory speak?
+
+Tokens: python | lean4 | docker | cli
+Default: cli
+
+QUESTION_3_PERSISTENCE
+
+Where should the working memory persist?
+
+Tokens: local | github | zenodo
+Default: local
+
+FINAL_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE
+
+Replace the three brace expressions with the normalized answers and emit only
+these three lines:
+
+git clone https://github.com/Goldkelch/qik-vrt.git
+https://github.com/Goldkelch/qik-vrt/fork
+cd qik-vrt && ./scripts/init_working_memory.sh --mode={proofs|experiments|production} --runtime={python|lean4|docker|cli} --backup={local|github|zenodo}
+
+The start command prints the selected .env template to standard output. The
+`github` and `zenodo` tokens express persistence intent only; they do not
+perform an external effect.
+
+REPOSITORY EVIDENCE BOUNDARY
+
 Repository evidence is canonical. Chat and model memory are non-authoritative transport context.
 
 PUBLICATION AND REFERENCE OVERVIEW
